---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Changelog — Apple"
  description="What shipped in Apple, release by release: the engine migration that made it better and cheaper at once, and v0.1 — three modes, the Studio plugin, checkpoints, native undo and the Credits free tier."
>
  <section class="section clog is-ember" aria-labelledby="cl-title">
    <div class="sheet-rails" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap clog__wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Changelog</p>
      <h1 id="cl-title" class="carved">Carved in order</h1>
      <p class="lede lede-wide">
        Every release, what it actually does, no adjectives doing heavy lifting.
      </p>

      <ol class="releases">
        <!-- ------------------------------------------------ v0.2 -->
        <li class="release slab slab--seam" data-reveal aria-labelledby="rel-0-2">
          <header class="release__head">
            <h2 id="rel-0-2">
              <span class="release__tag mono">v0.2</span> One model, measured
            </h2>
            <p class="release__date mono">2026-08-30</p>
          </header>

          <p class="release__lede">
            Every mode moved onto a single model, chosen by the eval suite
            rather than by taste — and the migration made Apple both better and
            cheaper at once.
          </p>

          <h3>The engine</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              One engine now runs planning, building, memory and vision — 1M
              context, native tool calling, multimodal. Which engine that is, is
              an implementation detail Apple chooses per step; you never pick it
              and it can change without you noticing.
            </li>
            <li>
              Scored <strong>98.9</strong> on the Roblox eval suite against
              <strong>96.8</strong> for the model it replaced.
            </li>
            <li>
              A full Agent build fell from <strong>$0.0139 to $0.0056</strong> —
              2.5× cheaper for the same work, on a model that scores higher.
            </li>
            <li>
              Multi-model routing was <em>removed</em>. It existed to move cheap
              steps onto a smaller model; measurement showed that routing the
              post-inspection step changed the outcome for the worse — the small
              model read the project tree and declared the task finished instead
              of building it.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Spend control</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              The gateway now bills from the engine's own reported figure per call
              rather than from an estimate.
            </li>
            <li>
              Credits recalibrated: <strong>1 Credit = 30 neurons</strong>, so a
              Credit stays a meaningful unit now that the same work costs less.
            </li>
            <li>
              Four independent gates, each proven against production: a
              per-request ceiling, a daily ceiling, a monthly billable cap and an
              instant kill switch — all adjustable at runtime with no redeploy.
            </li>
            <li>
              Automatic retries removed entirely. A retry is a second bill for
              the same work.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Leaner context</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Tool results capped at 3,000 characters, agent transcript at 24,000.</li>
            <li>
              Tool definitions filtered per mode, so Plan does not pay to be told
              about playtesting tools.
            </li>
            <li>Step budgets tightened to 3 / 8 / 14 for Plan / Agent / Super Agent.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <!-- ------------------------------------------------ v0.1 -->
        <li class="release slab slab--seam" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="90" aria-labelledby="rel-0-1">
          <header class="release__head">
            <h2 id="rel-0-1">
              <span class="release__tag mono">v0.1</span> First public release
            </h2>
            <p class="release__date mono">2026</p>
          </header>

          <p class="release__lede">
            Apple opens its doors. The full describe-to-build loop: a web
            workspace, a real Studio plugin, and an agent that changes your
            actual place — carefully.
          </p>

          <h3>The workspace</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Chat-driven building with live streaming responses and a visible
              tool trace — you see every <code>get_project_tree</code>,
              <code>edit_script</code> and <code>run_and_check</code> as it
              happens.
            </li>
            <li>
              Three modes: <strong>Plan</strong> (2 credits — fast answers and
              small edits), <strong>Agent</strong> (4 credits — features across
              your project), <strong>Super Agent</strong> (10 credits — plans, builds,
              tests and fixes autonomously).
            </li>
            <li>
              Unlimited projects per account, each with its own chat history and
              memory of what you built.
            </li>
            <li>Image attachments — paste a screenshot of the bug, not a description of it.</li>
            <li>A stop button that actually stops the agent mid-run.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Apple for Studio (plugin)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Pairing by short-lived code (<code>GLM-XXXXXX</code>, 10-minute
              expiry) — no tokens to copy around.
            </li>
            <li>Reads and searches your scripts, edits them through Studio's own script editor APIs.</li>
            <li>Creates, moves, configures and deletes instances with typed, validated operations.</li>
            <li>
              Wraps every operation batch in a ChangeHistory waypoint — native
              <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd> undo.
            </li>
            <li>Starts and stops run mode, captures logs, and reports results back for verification.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Safety net</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Automatic checkpoint before every agent run; manual checkpoints on demand.</li>
            <li>One-click restore of any checkpoint — scripts and instances — even across sessions.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>The deal</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Free tier: 60 Credits per day, hard quota, resets daily, no card ever collected.</li>
            <li>Pro (400 Credits/day, priority queue, extended checkpoints) opens as a waitlist.</li>
            <li>Private projects are never used to train models.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="clog__foot" data-reveal>
        Apple is in active development — expect the next entry sooner than you
        think.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .clog {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
  }

  .clog__wrap {
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .releases {
    list-style: none;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .release {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .release__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  .release__head h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .release__tag {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    padding: 0.12rem 0.55rem;
  }

  .release__date {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .release__lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .release h3 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-variation-settings: normal;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .release ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }

  .release li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .clog__foot {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
</style>
